// The owner's message to an agent (plan/design-two-systems.md, section 3; the first slice). TO is the agent written
// to, NAMES the @NAMEs in the words, ADDRESSED whether there were any. A message naming others is a thread for sure;
// otherwise the watcher's one call (intake) says whether the words are a one-off, belong on an open ticket, or are a
// new thread. If that call fails, coordd answers OneOff.
//
// - OneOff: the words go to TO as they are (`give`), and nothing is posted. The turn that answers them is kept by
//   reference, so the owner can make a run of one-offs a thread later (Keep).
// - Place(t): the words are posted on t as the owner's, naming TO.
// - Thread: the words are this ticket's first post, naming TO and every @NAME; then it rests at the hole, a place for
//   posts that nothing runs. An Edit fills the hole: `return OneOff` drops it, `return Kept` keeps it as it is.
//
// result Kept: the thread is over (what was asked on it is done, or the owner let it go); its posts stay as they are.
// result Moved(to): the owner's words belonged on ticket TO and were posted there; this thread holds nothing.
// result OneOff: the owner's words were a one-off to TO; nothing is kept on a ticket.
kind thread from base
  letter N
  form to: Agent, names: [Agent], text: Text, addressed: Named | Unnamed
  result Kept | Moved(to: Ticket) | OneOff
  pattern
    v <- match addressed {
      Named => return Thread
      Unnamed => step watcher intake(text, to)
    };
    match v {
      OneOff =>
        _ <- give to text;
        return OneOff
      Place(t) =>
        _ <- post text on t as owner naming to;
        return Moved(t)
      Thread =>
        _ <- post text as owner naming to, names;
        ...
      Unsure(ts) =>
        w <- step owner pick(text, ts);
        match w {
          Place(t) =>
            _ <- post text on t as owner naming to;
            return Moved(t)
          Thread =>
            _ <- post text as owner naming to, names;
            ...
        }
    }

on owner_message(m) open thread(m.to, m.names, m.text, m.addressed)
